  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 111 PM CDT Sat Aug 22 2026\n\nVery hot and dry conditions are forecast through the extended \nforecast through much of next week. An upper level ridge will remain \ncentered across southeast New Mexico through the middle of the week. \nThis will result in highs in the upper 90s to near 106 for much of \nthe area, so Heat Advisories are likely for the Big Country, Concho \nValley, and Heartland through at least the middle of next week. \nPortions of the Big Country, especially the northern counties, may \nreach 110 degrees Monday afternoon, so Extreme Heat Warnings may be \nneeded. The aforementioned upper level ridge begins to slowly shift \nwest by the end of next week, which may result in slightly \"less \nhot\" temperatures. Still, temperatures will continue to remain above \nnormal, in the upper 90s to near 103. \n\nWest Central Texas will be on the eastern periphery of the ridge \nlate next week, as the upper level ridge shifts west. This may allow \nfor the development of isolated to scattered showers and \nthunderstorms late next week. For now, continued low end (15-20%) \nrain chances as confidence remains low.",
